      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T17:09:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One thing that came up in discussions last year was a preference from Corentin/Michael to avoid having a separate Dawn API for MRSTSS and instead rely on DawnLoadResolveTexture to infer when it can be used. It\u0027s described in https://crbug.com/463893793#comment8 and is discussed a bit in that thread. Skia would still be allocating a transient MSAA texture to use as a color attachment but that texture should be lazily allocated. Internally I believe dawn would replace the color attachment with the single sampled resolve attachment plus MSRTSS struct so the transient MSAA texture isn\u0027t used and is hopefully free/very cheap.\n\nI\u0027m not sure if there was any further discussion on this front?",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "053abbb9_684169d7",
        "filename": "src/dawn/dawn.json",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 3172,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001591
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T18:59:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hm... I was under the impression that this was the route that the Graphite and Dawn teams has agreed on based on conversations with you, Corentin, and previous docs/comments.\n\nCorentin, what\u0027s your thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "74c636fe_02c332db",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab295fac_850946dd",
        "filename": "src/dawn/dawn.json",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 3172,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T20:00:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could have misunderstood the sentiment. FWIW I think this approach is fine, it has a benefit of not allocating a multi-sampled texture for use as the color attachment that will never get used. It\u0027s also a pretty simple API, minus the validation logic, so it wouldn\u0027t be too hard to change how we trigger MSRTSS in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "053abbb9_684169d7",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa22ce12_f76b97be",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/AttachmentState.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T15:56:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we have validation that the sample count must be consistent between all the attachments? Like they must be all 1 (if we don\u0027t allow mixing), or a mix of single sampled and the same sample count (we don\u0027t support other than 4 or 1 so the test could be just a TODO). Also validation that the DS attachment is the correct sample count (or is it MSRTSS as well? In which case we would need a test and to update [1])",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f37dafc_5f9c7ec3",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/AttachmentState.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001591
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T18:59:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do have validation to ensure that all color attachment sample counts are 1 when using MSRTSS. See [2].\n\nDepth/Stencil won\u0027t be MSRTSS. As pointed out in [this comment](https://g-issues.chromium.org/issues/463893793#comment12) DS isn\u0027t resolved in WebGPU, so there\u0027s no use case for preserving single-sample DS between render passes.",
      "parentUuid": "aa22ce12_f76b97be",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f5e5307_76534de8",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/AttachmentState.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T20:00:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Depth/Stencil won\u0027t be MSRTSS. As pointed out in this comment DS isn\u0027t resolved in WebGPU, so there\u0027s no use case for preserving single-sample DS between render passes.\n\nI thought Vulkan MSRTSS did apply to depth/stencil attachments? Does Dawn ensure that if msaaRenderToSingleSampledDesc-\u003eimplicitSampleCount \u003d\u003d 4 then depth/stencil texture will always have sampleCount\u003d4 so that MSRTSS never comes into play?",
      "parentUuid": "8f37dafc_5f9c7ec3",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
